{"name":"Honeysuckle Vine","hex":"#fbf1c8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"honeysuckle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of the many species of arching shrubs and climbing vines of the genus Lonicera in the Caprifoliaceae family, many with sweet-smelling, bell-shaped flowers.\n\n A light yellow color inspired by the color of honeysuckle blossoms.","A light yellow color inspired by the color of honeysuckle blossoms."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/honeysuckle"},{"term":"vine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any plant whose stem requires support and which climbs by tendrils or twining.","Any plant the stem of which creeps along the ground."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Honeysuckle","blocks":[{"text":"Honeysuckles are arching shrubs or twining vines in the genus Lonicera of the family Caprifoliaceae. The genus includes 158 species native to northern latitudes in North America, Eurasia, and North Africa."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Lonicera_caprifolium001.jpg/330px-Lonicera_caprifolium001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honeysuckle","wikidata":"Q156047"},{"title":"Vine","blocks":[{"text":"A vine is any plant with a growth habit of trailing or scandent stems, lianas, or runners. The word vine can also refer to such stems or runners themselves, for instance, when used in wicker work."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/%22A_Momordica_charantia-_bitter_guard_plant%22.jpg/330px-%22A_Momordica_charantia-_bitter_guard_plant%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vine","wikidata":"Q917284"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Honeysuckle-2.jpg/500px-Honeysuckle-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia